Who owns the accounts that account number 108 has sent money to? Give the five lowest owner ids in ascending order.

Typed QueryIntent handoff:
{"intent":{"acceptance_tests":["Returns exactly 5 rows; owner_ids are in ascending order; all returned owner_ids are distinct and valid"],"aggregation":["COUNT(*)"],"assumptions":["Account numbers are unique; owner_id is a numeric or sortable field; each account has exactly one owner"],"entities":["Account","Owner"],"expected_shape":["5 rows with columns: owner_id"],"ordering":["Owner.owner_id ASC"],"predicates":["Account.account_number = '108'"],"relationships":["Account-[:SENT_TO]->Account","Account-[:OWNED_BY]->Owner"],"uncertainties":["Whether account 108 exists; whether it has sent money to any accounts; whether those accounts have owners"]},"question":"Who owns the accounts that account number 108 has sent money to? Give the five lowest owner ids in ascending order."}

How many distinct accounts sit within two transfer hops upstream of account number 108 — that is, accounts from which money reaches 108 in one or two transfers?

Typed QueryIntent handoff:
{"intent":{"acceptance_tests":["Result is non-negative integer","Count includes accounts exactly 1 or 2 hops away upstream"],"aggregation":["COUNT(DISTINCT Account.id)"],"assumptions":["Transfers are directed from source to destination","Account numbers are unique identifiers"],"entities":["Account"],"expected_shape":"scalar count","ordering":[],"predicates":["Account.number = '108'","TRANSFERS_TO hops <= 2"],"relationships":["TRANSFERS_TO (direction: upstream)"],"uncertainties":["Whether transfers include self-loops or cycles","Whether account 108 itself is included in the count"]},"question":"How many distinct accounts sit within two transfer hops upstream of account number 108 \u2014 that is, accounts from which money reaches 108 in one or two transfers?"}

How many distinct ordered pairs of two *different* accounts owned by the same party have a direct transfer running from the first to the second? Count each pair once however many transfers run between them.

Typed QueryIntent handoff:
{"intent":{"acceptance_tests":["Count should be non-negative integer","No duplicate pairs counted","Pairs with transfers in opposite direction are separate if querying directed transfers"],"aggregation":["COUNT(DISTINCT (Account1.id, Account2.id))"],"assumptions":["Each account has exactly one owner party","Transfers are directed edges between accounts","Account ownership is stored and queryable"],"entities":["Account","Party"],"expected_shape":"Single scalar count value","ordering":[],"predicates":["Account1.id != Account2.id","Account1.owned_by = Account2.owned_by"],"relationships":["Account-[:OWNED_BY]->Party","Account-[:TRANSFER_TO]->Account"],"uncertainties":["Whether transfers are stored as direct edges or require path traversal","Handling of accounts with no transfers or same-account transfers"]},"question":"How many distinct ordered pairs of two *different* accounts owned by the same party have a direct transfer running from the first to the second? Count each pair once however many transfers run between them."}

Which party owns the largest number of distinct accounts that all send money into one single common account, where every one of those transfers is below the 10,000,000 reporting threshold? Give the owner id and how many of their accounts are involved.

